            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Franchise Tax Board of California, the dispute centers on whether one state can be compelled to answer in another state\u2019s courts."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "13c0c6a00e7e9bcb70cbe7a594a5bb7842588bd40d9b99bb47e7883c79615b87",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13c0c6a00e7e-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Historically, states have been understood not to be sued in the courts of other states."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "13c0c6a00e7e9bcb70cbe7a594a5bb7842588bd40d9b99bb47e7883c79615b87",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13c0c6a00e7e-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The case\u2019s financial stakes have fallen from a multimillion\u2011dollar dispute to roughly $100,000."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Professors Baude and Sachs",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "13c0c6a00e7e9bcb70cbe7a594a5bb7842588bd40d9b99bb47e7883c79615b87",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13c0c6a00e7e-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 28,
              "start": 28
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Professors Baude and Sachs, professors Baude and Sachs note a universal rule in the law of nations that has not been constitutionalized."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Chemerinsky",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "13c0c6a00e7e9bcb70cbe7a594a5bb7842588bd40d9b99bb47e7883c79615b87",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13c0c6a00e7e-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 50,
              "start": 50
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Mr. Chemerinsky argues that Congress has plenary power over Indian tribes, a principle that historically excludes state interference."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Chemerinsky",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "13c0c6a00e7e9bcb70cbe7a594a5bb7842588bd40d9b99bb47e7883c79615b87",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-13c0c6a00e7e-0002-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 51,
              "start": 51
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Chemerinsky, he also cites the Hilton v. South Carolina decision, emphasizing that adherence to precedent promotes stability and respect for judicial authority."
      }
    ],
